title: Warpline M1.9 shipped — the fabric is now an authenticated chain (schema-v2 pickId, fabric verify), reviewer SHIP 0.9
summary: 'Built and shipped the keystone from the 5-lens audit: the pickId identity contract v1→v2 (TD-2026-07-01-721), gating M1c. computePickId now folds parentPickId (chain link), binding.treeId (byte tamper-evidence), authoredBy.agentId (attribution), and merge second-parent + algo into the content-address — closing Aegis C1 (append-only-by-convention) and C2 (bait-and-switch bytes under a sealed meaning). New `warpline fabric verify` recomputes every pickId, walks the chain, and re-derives bindings; new rewriteFabric identity guard (closes H2) stops #grade from silently drifting identity fields. During build, caught a PRE-EXISTING drift (TD-2026-07-01-202): the real fabric was sealed under two historical rules and #grade overwrote a hashed field for seq 1–7 — resolved by try-known-rules verification + a pickId-pinned grandfather manifest (.warpline/fabric-legacy.json). Also fixed T-029 (pick fail-open). The migration is DOGFOODED: the real ledger now has live v2 strands (seq 15/16) anchoring the v1 tip, boundaryAnchored true, verify exits 0 with exactly 7 grandfathered strands. Independent verification + adversarial reviewer pass both confirm behavior (SHIP 0.9). 224/224 tests green. Local commits 67b8cf42 + 8daa5cb7, NOT pushed.'
